OpenEva is developed from Nodum, an MIT-licensed project.
Upstream source: https://github.com/nodummd/nodum
The original copyright and license terms are preserved in LICENSE.
OpenEva's product name and domain are https://openeva.ai.

The file editor implementation uses unmodified BlockNote (MPL-2.0), IronCalc
(MIT/Apache-2.0), PDF.js (Apache-2.0) and DOMPurify (Apache-2.0 OR MPL-2.0).
The build includes their available notices and source locations in
public/vendor/NOTICE.txt and adjacent license files. Package versions are pinned
in web/package-lock.json. No Tolaria source code is included in OpenEva.

Excel workbooks use Univer Sheets 0.25.1 (Apache-2.0), ExcelJS 4.4.0 (MIT),
and SheetJS CE 0.20.3 (Apache-2.0). Runtime and license files are bundled in
public/vendor/spreadsheet, loaded only when opening a workbook. Integration
patterns and the initial workbook/language adapters were adapted from the
user-provided OpenEvaSaaS project. Storage remains OpenEva's Rust/Git engine.
